.TH MIHOMO-SERVER 1 2026-10-04 "mihomo-server" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mihomo-server \- control your headless Mihomo instance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mihomo-server
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-api
.IR URL ]
.RB [ \-\-token\-file
.IR FILE ]
.I command
.RI [ argument ...]
.br
.B mihomo-server serve
.RI [ service-option ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mihomo-server
manages your own instance of the shared mihomo-server installation: the
systemd user service, subscriptions, proxy groups and nodes, the proxy mode,
the system-wide TUN and the Mihomo core.
.PP
Without
.BR \-\-api ,
commands act on the running systemd user unit
.I mihomo-server.service
of the invoking user and read its management address and token from that
service.  Service commands (start, stop, restart, enable, disable, info,
token, logs, purge) are performed by
.BR mihomo-server-user ,
which is installed alongside.
.PP
Wherever a subscription, group or node is expected, it may be given as its
exact name, its number in the corresponding list, its name in any case, or
any unique part of its name.  When an operand is omitted on a terminal, a
numbered list is shown to choose from.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Write machine-readable JSON to standard output instead of text.
.TP
.BI \-\-api " URL"
Use the management API at
.I URL
(for example a foreground service) instead of the systemd user instance.
Service commands start, stop and restart then control the core only.
.TP
.BI \-\-token\-file " FILE"
Read the management token from
.IR FILE .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Write a usage summary; after a command, describe that command.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Write the program version.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Service
.TP
.B status
Show the service and core state, the subscription in use, the proxy mode,
TUN, the proxy port and the management address.
.TP
.B start
Start the instance and wait until its core and API are ready.
.TP
.B stop
Stop the instance.
.TP
.B restart
Restart the instance and wait until it is ready.
.TP
.B enable
Start the instance now and at every boot (alias:
.BR init ).
.TP
.B disable
Stop the instance and do not start it at boot.  Data is kept.
.TP
.B info
Show the management login address, token file, proxy port and paths.
.TP
.B token
Write the management token.
.TP
.BR logs " [" \fIjournalctl-option\fR ...]
Follow the service journal, or pass the options to
.BR journalctl (1),
for example
.BR "logs \-n 100" .
.TP
.BR purge " [" \-y ]
Delete your instance data, configuration and slot.
.SS Subscriptions
.TP
.BR "sub " [ list ]
List subscriptions; the one in use is marked with
.BR * .
.TP
.BR "sub use " [\fIsubscription\fR]
Use (apply) a subscription.
.TP
.BR "sub update " [\fIsubscription\fR...]
Download remote subscriptions again; all remote ones when none is given.
.TP
.BR "sub add " \fIsource\fR " [" \-n " \fIname\fR] [" \-\-use ]
Import an http(s) subscription URL or a local YAML file.
.TP
.BR "sub remove " \fIsubscription\fR " [" \-y ]
Delete a subscription.
.SS Proxies
.TP
.BR "proxy " [ list ]
List proxy groups and their selected nodes; the main group is marked with
.BR * .
.TP
.BI "proxy list " group
List the nodes of
.I group
with their last measured delay.
.TP
.BR "proxy select " [[\fIgroup\fR] " \fInode\fR]"
Select
.I node
in
.IR group ,
by default in the main group (GLOBAL in global mode, otherwise the group
named Proxies, otherwise the first selector).
.TP
.BR "proxy test " [\fItarget\fR] " [" \-\-url " \fIURL\fR] [" \-\-timeout " \fIms\fR]"
Test the delay of every node of a group, or of one node; the main group
by default.  Results are sorted, fastest first.
.TP
.BI "proxy unfix " group
Let an automatic (url-test or fallback) group choose again.
.SS Mode, TUN and core
.TP
.BR "mode " [ rule | global | direct ]
Show or set the proxy mode.
.TP
.BR "tun " [ on | off ]
Show or switch the TUN.  It is system-wide: the first member of group
mihomo-tun to enable it holds it until they disable it.
.TP
.BR "core " [ version ]
Show the installed and running Mihomo version.
.TP
.BR "core update " [ \-\-alpha "] [" \-\-force ]
Upgrade the core of this instance; it is rolled back when it fails.
.SS Installation
.TP
.BR update " [" \-\-force ]
Download and run the latest release installer, unless the installed
release is already the latest.  Requires sudo.
.TP
.BR uninstall " [" \-\-purge "] [" \-y ]
Remove the shared installation for all users; with
.BR \-\-purge ,
also every user's data.  Requires sudo.
.TP
.BR serve " [" \fIservice-option\fR ...]
Run the management service in the foreground; this is what the systemd
unit runs.  See
.BR "mihomo-server serve \-\-help" .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MIHOMO_SERVER_API
Default for
.BR \-\-api .
.TP
.B MIHOMO_SERVER_TOKEN_FILE
Default for
.BR \-\-token\-file .
.TP
.B MIHOMO_SERVER_INSTALLER
Installer path or URL used by
.B update
and
.BR uninstall .
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directories of the configuration and data files.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mihomo-server/env
Startup settings, such as
.B MIHOMO_SERVER_LISTEN
and
.BR MIHOMO_SERVER_PUBLIC_ORIGIN .
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/mihomo-server/
Subscriptions, settings, core and the
.I management-token
file.
.TP
.I /opt/mihomo-server/current/
The installed program.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The operation failed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid usage.
.TP
.B 3
.B status
only: the instance is not running.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mihomo-server status
mihomo-server sub add https://example.com/sub \-n work \-\-use
mihomo-server proxy test
mihomo-server proxy select \(aqTokyo 03\(aq
mihomo-server proxy select AI 3
mihomo-server mode global
mihomo-server tun on
mihomo-server logs \-n 50 \-\-no\-pager
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
